@startuml 07-discovery
!include _style.iuml
title Discovery — the sources found for the interests of a profile

class "server start" as ServerStart <<other feature>> {
    + resumeInterrupted()
}
class profileService <<other feature>> {
    + store()
    + rediscover()
    + get()
}
class briefingService <<other feature>> {
    + write()
}
package "Business" {
    class discoveryService {
        + start()
        + discover()
        + prune()
        + phaseOf()
        + resumeInterrupted()
    }
    class sourceService <<other feature>> {
        + knownMedia()
    }
    class ingestService <<other feature>> {
        + run()
        + searchesOfUser()
    }
    class feedbackService <<other feature>> {
        + of()
    }
}
note right of discoveryService
    Two steps: the media Google News names
    for each interest, saved and read at once
    (phase 'google'), then the press only
    Media Cloud names (phase 'press'). Each
    step tries per interest and per language
    with its own budget. Lives in memory: a
    restart starts it again
end note
package "Data" as Data {
    class profileModel {
        + get()
        + interestsForDiscovery()
        + setDiscovery()
        + discovering()
        + removedSources()
        + keptSources()
        + addProfileFeeds()
        + deleteProfileFeeds()
        + profileFeedRelevance()
    }
    class feedModel {
        + userFeedUrls()
        + countUserFeeds()
        + trustedFeedUrls()
    }
}
note bottom of profileModel
    user_feeds origin 'profile'; status in
    user_profiles.discovery_status (running,
    done, failed). The interests of a
    project are not looked for
end note
package "The media of an interest" as Media {
    class googleNews {
        + search()
    }
    class mediaCloud {
        + mediaCloudEnabled()
        + mediaFor()
        + knownFeeds()
    }
    class profileAi {
        + parseSearch()
        + confirmOnSubject()
    }
    class publicUrl {
        + nameOf()
    }
    class language {
        + readerLanguage()
    }
}
note bottom of mediaCloud
    Every word of a search (AND), in its
    language, over 30 days, in the press of
    its countries; 2 news at least. 2 searches
    a minute, a refusal pauses it 15 minutes,
    an answer kept a day. Off without
    MEDIACLOUD_API_TOKEN
end note
note bottom of profileAi
    The AI reads the 12 newest titles the
    vectors put on the interests: the feed
    stays on 2 it confirms
end note
package "The feeds of a medium" as Feeds {
    class feedFinder {
        + findFeeds()
        + isOnSubject()
        + subjectScore()
    }
    class meaningJudge {
        + judgeOf()
    }
    class embedder {
        + parseVector()
    }
}
note bottom of feedFinder
    Kept when 2 of its last 30 news reach
    0.45 with an interest. Looks in the page,
    the sections, Feedly, the news sitemap
    and RSS-Bridge: see 05-sources
end note
package "The budget" as Budget {
    class allocation {
        + tryPerLanguage()
        + pressSearches()
        + allocate()
        + staleFeeds()
    }
    class feedLimits {
        + bridgeRoom()
        + withinBridgeRoom()
    }
}
note bottom of allocation
    20 new feeds a discovery, 60 for the
    profile. Removed: no news on the profile
    in 14 days, once 14 days old or 30 news;
    the kept and trusted ones stay
end note
class "Google News" as GoogleNewsApi <<external>>
class "Media Cloud" as MediaCloudApi <<external>>
class "Embedder (bge-m3)" as Embedder <<external>>
class "Ollama (gemma4:31b)" as Ollama <<external>>
class "PostgreSQL + pgvector" as PostgreSQL <<external>>

googleNews -[hidden]down- mediaCloud
feedFinder -[hidden]down- meaningJudge
allocation -[hidden]down- feedLimits

ServerStart --> discoveryService
profileService --> discoveryService
briefingService --> discoveryService
discoveryService --> sourceService
discoveryService --> ingestService
discoveryService --> feedbackService
discoveryService ----> Data
discoveryService --> Media
discoveryService --> Feeds
discoveryService ----> Budget
mediaCloud --> publicUrl
googleNews --> GoogleNewsApi
mediaCloud --> MediaCloudApi
profileAi --> Ollama
meaningJudge --> Embedder
Data --> PostgreSQL
@enduml
